# Appendix: Failed Strategies

The following approaches were tested but did not improve performance:

1. Lower Threshold (< 0.40)
- Increased false positives
- Reduced leaderboard score

2. Aggressive Water Suppression
- Removed true flood pixels
- Decreased Flood IoU

3. Morphological Operations (Dilation/Blur)
- Distorted segmentation boundaries
- Reduced prediction quality

4. Test-Time Augmentation (Flip Averaging)
- Introduced noise in predictions
- No consistent improvement

5. Over-training / Additional Epochs
- Caused overfitting
- No improvement in validation performance

Conclusion:
The final model uses a balanced threshold (0.40) with controlled water suppression, which provided the best score (0.2000).
